# Craftista – Infrastructure (Terraform)

Infrastructure-as-Code for the **DevOps Certification Project**: provisions the complete VM landscape for the [Craftista application](../devops-certification-project) on a **Proxmox VE** host using Terraform.

> Final project of the **DevOps Engineer Certification Program (Liora)**
> Authors: **Florian Munkelt · Jan Krüger**

## What it creates

From a single `terraform apply`, the configuration builds a template-and-clone setup on the Proxmox host `XX.XX.XX.XX` (**TEMPORARY REDACTION**):

1. Downloads the official **Ubuntu 22.04 (Jammy) cloud image** to the Proxmox datastore
2. Creates a **VM template** (`ubuntu-template`) from it – never started, marked `template = true`
3. Clones the template **4×** into the running cluster VMs

| VM | IP | Role |
|---|---|---|
| cluster-node-0 | XX.XX.XX.XX | k3s master (control plane) |
| cluster-node-1 | XX.XX.XX.XX | k3s worker |
| cluster-node-2 | XX.XX.XX.XX | k3s worker |
| cluster-node-3 | XX.XX.XX.XX | PostgreSQL (outside the cluster) |

All VMs sit on the private `XX.XX.XX.XX/XX` network behind the Proxmox host (gateway `XX.XX.XX.XX`) and are **not reachable from the internet** – access only via port forwarding / SSH jump host. (**TEMPORARY REDACTION**)

## VM Specification

- Ubuntu 22.04 LTS cloud image · machine `q35` · UEFI (**OVMF** + EFI disk)
- **2 vCPU · 8 GB RAM · 20 GB disk** (datastore `vmdata`, VirtIO, iothread, discard)
- Network bridge `vmbr0` · static IPv4 per clone index · DNS `1.1.1.1`
- **cloud-init**: user `XX` (**TEMPORARY REDACTION**) with the Proxmox host's SSH public key injected

## Requirements

- Terraform with provider **`bpg/proxmox ~> 0.111`**
- Proxmox API credentials set as **environment variables** on the host
- SSH agent access as `XX` (**TEMPORARY REDACTION**; used by the provider to import the cloud image)

## Usage

```bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply -parallelism=1 -auto-approve
```

> `-parallelism=1` is required: concurrent clone operations from the same template are unreliable on the Proxmox API.

